      "cephalopod_ethics_graphic_novel": "Cephalopod ethics graphic novel",
      "cephalopod_evolution_three_solutions_t": "Cephalopod Evolution: Three Solutions to the Same Problem",
      "cephalopod_evolution_timeline_mural": "Cephalopod evolution timeline mural",
      "cephalopod_eye_vertebrate_eye_independ": "Cephalopod eye + vertebrate eye independently evolved similar structures (cornea, lens, iris, retina) — one of the strongest examples of convergent evolution.",
      "cephalopod_eye_vs_vertebrate_eye": "Cephalopod Eye vs. Vertebrate Eye",
      "cephalopod_eyes_are_camera_style_with_": "Cephalopod eyes are camera-style with a lens + retina, structurally similar to vertebrate eyes but evolved INDEPENDENTLY (convergent evolution). Key differences: their photoreceptors point TOWARD the light (vs ours pointing away → blind spot in humans). Most cephalopods are color-blind despite producing the most varied skin displays in nature. Theory: they detect polarized light (we can't) + may have skin-distributed color sensors (opsins in the skin itself).",
      "cephalopod_eyes_are_converged_with_ver": "Cephalopod eyes are CONVERGED with vertebrate eyes — they evolved independently to produce similar structures (lens, retina, iris). This is one of the most famous examples of convergent evolution.",
      "cephalopod_foraging_tactics": "Cephalopod foraging tactics",
      "cephalopod_fossils_are_typically_found": "Cephalopod fossils are typically found in MARINE sediments — they have never lived in freshwater (with the partial exception of some brackish-tolerant species).",
      "cephalopod_fossils_show_clear_evidence": "Cephalopod fossils show clear evidence of predator-prey co-evolution with fish — when fish jaws strengthened in the Devonian, ammonoid shells thickened.",
      "cephalopod_functional_morphology": "Cephalopod functional morphology",
      "cephalopod_genome_sequencing_shows_22_": "Cephalopod genome sequencing shows ~22% of cephalopod-specific genes have no clear vertebrate orthologs — they evolved entirely independently.",
      "cephalopod_genomes_are_spectacularly_l": "Cephalopod genomes are SPECTACULARLY large + complex compared to other invertebrates. Octopus bimaculoides genome is ~2.7 Gb, with expanded gene families for nervous system development.",
      "cephalopod_glossary": "📖 Cephalopod glossary",
      "cephalopod_imagery_in_modern_poetry_ad": "Cephalopod imagery in modern poetry (Adrienne Rich, Mary Oliver, others).",
      "cephalopod_impact": "🐙 Cephalopod impact",
      "cephalopod_ink_contains_active_compoun": "Cephalopod ink contains active compounds being investigated for antibacterial properties — particularly against marine pathogens.",
      "cephalopod_ink_has_been_used_as_a_dye_": "Cephalopod ink has been used as a dye + writing ink since antiquity. The word \"sepia\" (a brown color) comes from the cuttlefish genus Sepia.",
      "cephalopod_ink_has_been_used_in_writin": "Cephalopod ink has been used in writing + art for over 2000 years. The word \"sepia\" (a brown pigment) comes from the cuttlefish genus Sepia.",
      "cephalopod_ink_production_chemistry_fu": "Cephalopod ink: production, chemistry, functions and applications",
      "cephalopod_inspired_aliens_are_now_a_r": "Cephalopod-inspired aliens are now a recurring science-fiction trope. The Heptapods of \"Arrival\" (2016) use radial language reminiscent of octopus distributed intelligence. \"Soma\" video game features deep-sea AI in cephalopod-like bodies. The aliens in \"Annihilation\" reference cephalopod chromatophore biology.",
      "cephalopod_inspired_architecture_has_e": "Cephalopod-inspired architecture has emerged — some buildings + bridges use shell-like load distribution principles derived from nautilus shell biomechanics.",
      "cephalopod_inspired_soft_sculpture": "Cephalopod-inspired soft sculpture",
      "cephalopod_inspired_song_or_poem": "Cephalopod-inspired song or poem",
      "cephalopod_intelligence_camouflage_ink": "Cephalopod intelligence + camouflage + ink + tool use ALL appear to have evolved AFTER the loss of the external shell. Vulnerability drove behavioral complexity.",
      "cephalopod_intelligence_evolved_indepe": "Cephalopod intelligence evolved independently from vertebrate intelligence. What might have driven its evolution?",
      "cephalopod_iridophore_cells_use_stacks": "Cephalopod iridophore cells use stacks of reflectin protein platelets to make BLUE and GREEN — structural color, not pigment color.",
      "cephalopod_jet_noise": "Cephalopod jet noise",
      "cephalopod_lab": "Cephalopod Lab",
