      "most_accessible_activity_for_nearly_an": "Most accessible activity for nearly any body.",
      "most_people_s_relationship_with_food_h": "Most people's relationship with food has bumps. There's a difference between an OCCASIONAL hard day with food (which is part of being human) and a PATTERN that interferes with your life or your health.",
      "most_people_with_eating_disorders_reco": "Most people with eating disorders recover, especially when they get support EARLIER rather than later. Recovery isn't linear — it has hard days, setbacks, and slow improvement — but the trajectory is real and well-documented.",
      "most_us_teens_get_only_half_this_fiber": "Most US teens get only ~half this. Fiber feeds gut microbes.",
      "mostly_sitting": "Mostly sitting",
      "mouth_stomach_intestines": "Mouth → stomach → intestines",
      "move_four_sliders_carb_protein_fat_fib": "Move four sliders (carb / protein / fat / fiber). Predict how the macro pattern shifts the energy state — ketogenic, low-carb, balanced, high-carb, sugar-dominant. Includes a satiety estimate and a fiber-adjusted glycemic index proxy. Discrete states, no score, no reveal — you mark your own understanding.",
      "my_nutrition_kit": "My Nutrition Kit",
      "my_nutrition_kit_2": "My Nutrition Kit",
      "naming_a_pattern_out_loud_with_a_frien": "Naming a pattern out loud, with a friend or trusted adult, is one of the fastest ways to recognize it for what it is. \"That video felt weird, did you see it?\" is enough to start.",
      "nationaleatingdisorders_org_research_b": "(nationaleatingdisorders.org) — research-backed guidance and free educator toolkits",
