      "type_your_name_a_word_or_a_short_phras": "Type your name, a word, or a short phrase. See it set in five typefaces from across the printed centuries. Each one was the default of its era. Your name in Blackletter would have looked like a 1455 contract. In Helvetica it would look like a 1980s passport.",
      "typography_inquiry_predict_the_legibil": "🔬 Typography Inquiry — Predict the Legibility",
      "typography_today": "Typography Today",
      "ukiyo_e_pictures_of_the_floating_world": "Ukiyo-e (\"pictures of the floating world\") were full-color woodblock prints made by teams: designer drew the master image, carvers cut a separate block for each color, printer registered each block onto the same paper in sequence. A single complex Hokusai print might use 15-20 blocks. The technical sophistication was unmatched globally until photogravure in the 1880s.",
      "ulysses_james_joyce": "Ulysses (James Joyce)",
