      "a_field_of_mirrors_called_heliostats_f": "A field of mirrors called heliostats focuses sunlight onto a central tower receiver. Molten salt circulates through the receiver, heating to 565 degrees Celsius. Hot salt is stored in an insulated tank. Demand-side, hot salt flows through a heat exchanger to make steam, which spins a turbine and generator. Cold salt returns to a second tank to be reheated.",
      "a_high_renewable_future_depends_just_a": "A high-renewable future depends just as much on smart-grid software, transmission, and demand-side flexibility as it does on the next solar farm or wind turbine. The \"boring\" infrastructure pieces are where most of the engineering happens.",
      "a_home_consumes_1_kw_continuous_on_ave": "A home consumes ~1 kW continuous on average. So this array could power roughly ",
      "a_maine_specialty": " — a Maine specialty.",
      "a_note_on_scope": "⚠ A note on scope",
      "a_partly_submerged_chamber_traps_a_col": "A partly submerged chamber traps a column of air above the rising and falling sea surface. As waves push the water up and down inside the chamber, the trapped air is forced in and out through a Wells turbine — which spins the same direction regardless of which way the air flows. The turbine drives a generator.",
      "a_refrigeration_cycle_that_moves_heat_": "A refrigeration cycle that moves heat between the constant-temperature ground and a home. In winter, evaporator absorbs heat from the ground loop; compressor raises temperature; condenser releases heat to the home; expansion valve resets the cycle. COP 3 to 5 means 3 to 5 units of heat moved per unit of electricity used.",
      "a_reservoir_behind_a_concrete_dam_stor": "A reservoir behind a concrete dam stores water at high elevation. Water flows down through the penstock, spins a turbine, drives a generator, and exits the tailrace. Power equals density times gravity times head times flow times efficiency.",
      "a_typical_home_rooftop_array_20_40_m_a": "A typical home rooftop array: 20–40 m². A megawatt utility array: ~5,000 m².",
      "a_typical_maine_2_story_has_30_60_m_of": "A typical Maine 2-story has 30–60 m² of usable south slope. 1 m² ≈ 10.8 ft².",
      "a_typical_maine_commute_30_mi_day_adds": ". A typical Maine commute (~30 mi/day) adds ~7–10 kWh/day to your home load — significant for solar sizing, and EVs unlock V2G later.",
